ess and  power lifting  because like the first equipped 800  pound bench press didn't fall all that  long ago um  you have like 30 seconds of input so i  can just really quick google when the  first 800 pound equip bench pressure  yeah yeah um  no i mean looking at this video uh like  you said it initially you weren't the  you weren't just like some rogue actor  saying i call bs on these lifts i mean  there are a lot of people in the  comments as he was posting videos into  the mid and high 700s saying i don't  know are we sure about this  but yeah you look at this video of him  benching 804 the way the bar is moving  looks like it's got at least 803 pounds  yeah like i i'm i'm definitely a  believer and i think a lot of people are  coming around to that perspective  yeah so the the first 800 pound equipped  binge press was tim isaac in 1999  which  isn't that it isn't all that long ago um  and so  i don't know it's this is this is making  my head spin like 700  seemed to be the final frontier for the  bench press at least in terms of 100  pound barriers  and then when julius maddox started  chipping away at it pushing it up into  760 770 it's like oh [ __ ] 800 is gonna  happen  but then  i don't know there's a part of me deep  within my soul that wants to say we have  seen the final hundred pound barrier  fall for the raw bench press  but like i don't know man who's to say  uh  will will 900 ever happen or is this the  final frontier like with with the mile  for example when a sub four minute mile  happened  you knew that that was the last minute  barrier just like due to  certain  constraints within human physiology um  unless just like track surfaces and the  equipment allowed changes dramatically  we're never going to see a sub 3 mile  but  like and same thing with the marathon  it's like sub two is it yeah we're we're  not gonna see a sub one marathon yeah  it's ridiculous  but yeah with  with the bench press i don't i don't  know what those physiological  con